---
source: tests/doctor.rs
expression: text
---
ricepilot doctor: no problems, 7 hazards. nothing was changed; the commands are for you to run.

HAZARD 1 of 7: <HOME>/.local/state/ricepilot/attic
  has grown to 3.0 GiB in 2 entries; the newest, <TS>, holds 0 B.
  rule: SAFETY.md R2 (displaced; only `gc` removes, D61)

  everything a switch, rollback or adopt displaced is here: nothing but
  `gc` removes anything, and gc only what you name. the largest:
    <TS>  3.0 GiB  (1 item)
    <TS>  0 B  (2 items)

  it can hold your own directories — an adopt moves the original here (D49).
  gc keeps one unless a profile holds an identical copy and the path is
  ricepilot's link, and says why it keeps anything; read that before you answer.

  run:
    du -sh <HOME>/.local/state/ricepilot/attic/*
    # lists every entry, and why each could go or is kept; removes nothing
    ricepilot gc
    # asks for each candidate's name to be typed back, and removes only those
    ricepilot gc --commit

HAZARD 2 of 7: <HOME>/.local/state/ricepilot/verify
  holds 21 scratch copies, 231 B in all.
  rule: D55 (the scratch copy stays, as the record of what was parsed)

  every `plan`, `switch` and `rollback` into a profile with a hyprland.conf
  leaves one. the oldest is <TS>, the newest <TS>. only `gc` reclaims them.

  run:
    du -sh <HOME>/.local/state/ricepilot/verify
    # lists them; `--commit` asks for each one's name before it removes it
    ricepilot gc

HAZARD 3 of 7: <HOME>/.local/bin/hypr-session
  writes into ~/.config/hypr, which ricepilot links.
  rule: SAFETY.md R3 (nothing writes into a profile) — this script does

  on every call it creates ~/.config/hypr/sessions — through ricepilot's link, so
  inside a profile's tree. `verify` then reports the profile as changed,
  and the directory travels with the profile.

  the patch, for you to apply; ricepilot does not edit your scripts:
    --- <HOME>/.local/bin/hypr-session
    +++ <HOME>/.local/bin/hypr-session
    @@ line 3 @@
    -  export SESSION_DIR="$HOME/.config/hypr/sessions"
    +  export SESSION_DIR="${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/hypr/sessions"

  run:
    $EDITOR <HOME>/.local/bin/hypr-session

HAZARD 4 of 7: <HOME>/.local/share/caelestia
  is the root of `caelestia`, and caelestia-cli migrates from it.
  rule: NOT-POSSIBLE.md#running-rice-installers

  `caelestia install` and `caelestia update` can delete this whole tree through
  caelestia-cli's legacy-migration path, and caelestia's install.fish
  overwrites by deleting first. ricepilot never runs either. if you do, run
  `ricepilot doctor` afterwards: the links they turn into directories show
  up as problems.

  run:
    # what the clone holds that is committed nowhere: the part an installer loses
    git -C <HOME>/.local/share/caelestia status

HAZARD 5 of 7: /home
  is not snapshotted.
  rule: NOT-POSSIBLE.md#snapshotting

  snapper has 1 config for other subvolumes: root.

  everything ricepilot moves lives under /home, and nothing there is covered
  by a snapshot.

  ricepilot cannot take one: a snapshot needs root, and ricepilot never
  runs sudo. on a btrfs /home this is the command, as root:

  run:
    snapper -c home create-config /home

HAZARD 6 of 7: <HOME>/sys/proc/4242
  `caelestia shell -d` is running (pid 4242).
  rule: DESIGN.md §3, why `generated` exists

  caelestia's theme engine rewrites its generated files with a temporary
  file and a rename, which replaces a symlink at any of those paths and
  changes files inside the profile's tree. expect `verify` to report them,
  and declare them `generated` or `volatile` in the profile. ricepilot does
  not stop the shell.

HAZARD 7 of 7: <HOME>/sys/proc/4243
  `caelestia resizer -d` is running (pid 4243).
  rule: DESIGN.md §3, why `generated` exists

  caelestia's theme engine rewrites its generated files with a temporary
  file and a rename, which replaces a symlink at any of those paths and
  changes files inside the profile's tree. expect `verify` to report them,
  and declare them `generated` or `volatile` in the profile. ricepilot does
  not stop the resizer.

not checked, or worth knowing:
  - profile `new`: <HOME>/rice/new/hypr/hyprland.lua is a Lua config, which nothing can check before a login (NOT-POSSIBLE.md#verify-lua-config)
  - profile `old`: <HOME>/rice/old/hypr/hyprland.lua is a Lua config, which nothing can check before a login (NOT-POSSIBLE.md#verify-lua-config)
  - profile `caelestia`: no manifest has been recorded for it yet, so its tree was not compared with anything
  - profile `old`: no manifest has been recorded for it yet, so its tree was not compared with anything

ok: no interrupted operation; 3 owned links intact; the ledger and the manifests agree; 2 hypr trees have an entry file; 1 profile tree matches its recorded manifest; rescue.sh restores generation 0000 and parses; no interrupted gc
